I have a complicated relationship with my mother.
label string2
She never accepted me being queer. And she didn't believe me when I needed it the most.
label string3
Hate and fear has been cultivated in the society we grew up.
label string4
Just like I never truly know who I am. I never truly know if she actually loves me or hates me
label string5
But I still remember the song she sang me to put me to sleep. I remember smiles, warmth, hugs. Sakha kisses when you kiss your relatives by smelling them
label string6
I don't know how much of all these complications is just life or colonialism. Or other structures.
label string7
I remember. So it means I resist
[signal arg="mixing_ended"]
[end_timeline]